                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4DbXpQDSfPJ9_RQCylcr-48" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#2e5a2e&quot;&gt;✓ FIXED — the system keeps the customer informed of their request status on a regular cadence, reducing confusion and delivering a better user experience.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#2e5a2e;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;size=14;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1215" y="638" width="250" height="105" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="4DbXpQDSfPJ9_RQCylcr-49" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#2e5a2e&quot;&gt;✓ FIXED — requests are never forgotten. Unanswered centers are followed up on until the booking is resolved (no more &quot;one-and-done&quot;), and every request that stalls escalates to a human with reminders until it is closed out.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#2e5a2e;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;size=14;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1215" y="760" width="250" height="105" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="mELlnSKkdkoz0Xh0CBPf-1" value="&lt;div&gt;Questions:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. Expected usage per month =&amp;gt; ~ 5000&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Expected spikes per month&amp;nbsp; =&amp;gt; up to 100&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Is there any database or service to tell us if an user needs additional paperwork? ~ is donde per state this would be transparent for us&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. For each service quote is there any negotiation involved? ~ No&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;5. We need to take a look at regulation : Do we need to tell the client is talking to an AI agent? - We will need to do an spike on this ~ needs spike&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;6. How does work orders works, could be autogenerated or are they generated by a human? ~ this will be handle by Yoguesh though an api&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;7. How are we going to scalate to human through an email, zendesk ticket? ~ they wil give us an api&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;8. confirmation to users will be issued via sms / email or also voice agent? ~ TBD&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#3b5b8c;dashed=1;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=8;arcSize=6;shadow=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="635" y="-350" width="465" height="250" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="mELlnSKkdkoz0Xh0CBPf-3" value="&lt;div&gt;Acceses we need :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1. AWS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Current app form and IVR&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Github&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. Database or microservice for services center&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. recommended backend python&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#3b5b8c;dashed=1;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=8;arcSize=6;shadow=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="111" y="-490" width="465" height="250" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
